@startuml InquiryConsent

title Inquiry Consent API Sequence

' Leading SQL apostrophes use &#39; so PlantUML preserves literals; parity compares decoded SQL.

' Visual style
skinparam defaultFontName "Sarabun"
skinparam defaultFontSize 14
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam roundcorner 10
skinparam sequence {
    ArrowColor #475569
    ArrowFontColor #334155
    LifeLineBorderColor #CBD5E1
    LifeLineBackgroundColor #F8FAFC
    ParticipantBorderColor #94A3B8
    ParticipantBackgroundColor #F1F5F9
    ParticipantFontColor #0F172A
    GroupBorderColor #94A3B8
    GroupBackgroundColor #F8FAFC
    GroupFontColor #334155
}

' Do not show participant footers at the bottom of the diagram
hide footbox

actor "User" as user
box "Frontend" #F8FAFC
    participant "Inquiry Consent Page" as page
end box
box "Web API" #F8FAFC
    participant "API" as api
    participant "Application" as app
    participant "Domain" as domain
    participant "Infrastructure" as infra
end box
box "Database" #F8FAFC
    database "t_user_access_token" as t_user_access_token
    database "t_consent" as t_consent
    database "m_consent_type" as m_consent_type
end box

user -> page: Read all consents with optional filters and pagination
activate page
    page -> api: GET v1/consent (Bearer JWT, UTC timestamp; query only)
    activate api
        api -> app: [**InquiryConsentQueryHandler**] Process request
        activate app
            note over app, infra
                Execution order: validate query/header/body and checked pagination (400) -> verify JWT/roles (401) -> begin
                read-only repeatable-read transaction -> fresh now/expiry -> joined current credential/user (401) -> claims
                permission (403) -> count -> optional page -> consent type names -> complete mapping -> COMMIT -> 200. Every
                post-BEGIN rejection rolls back.
            end note
            app -> app: Generate requestId; validate UTC timestamp, known single query keys/no body, UUID id, positive signed Int64 pages/default 1/10/pageSize <=100 and ACTIVE/INACTIVE/LOCKED/ARCHIVED filter
            note over app, infra
                Reject unknown/repeated keys and malformed header/query with 400 E10001 before SQL. Generate requestId if
                omitted. Supplied id is a non-empty UUID, never null; omitted id is typed SQL NULL. pageIndex/pageSize are
                positive signed 64-bit integers, default 1/10 only when omitted, pageSize at most 100. Compute checked
                offset = (pageIndex - 1) * pageSize and reject parse/offset overflow beyond nonnegative BIGINT with 400.
                Explicit empty/null-like values do not become defaults.
            end note
            app -> app: Compute checked offset = (pageIndex - 1) * pageSize; reject numeric/offset overflow beyond nonnegative BIGINT
            alt Invalid input or pagination overflow
                break Reject this inquiry
                    app -> api: HTTP 400 E10001
                    api -> page: Show failure without a partial consent page
                    page -> user: Display failure; no consent data
                end break
            else Check passed
            end
            app -> app: Verify JWT signature/issuer/audience/expiry/UUID sub and the roles claim as unique non-empty strings
            alt Missing/invalid JWT or malformed roles
                break Reject this inquiry
                    app -> api: HTTP 401 E10002 Invalid or expired access token.
                    api -> page: Show failure without a partial consent page
                    page -> user: Display failure; no consent data
                end break
            else Check passed
            end
            app -> app: callerUserId = verified sub; accessTokenHash = SHA-256 exact JWT
            app -> app: Bind omitted id/searchPattern/rowStatus as typed SQL NULL; supplied searchPattern = percent + search + percent, preserving ILIKE wildcards
            app -> infra: BEGIN REPEATABLE READ READ ONLY
            note over app, infra
                Verify Bearer JWT signature/issuer/audience/expiry/UUID sub and the roles claim before BEGIN. roles must be
                an array of unique non-empty strings, including [] (JWT payload of 2026-11-13). Missing/malformed roles is
                generic 401 E10002, never an empty-list or live-grant fallback. Derive callerUserId only from verified sub
                and accessTokenHash as SHA-256 of the exact presented JWT; do not accept caller ids or isPlatformAdmin flags
                from requests.
                Require matching token hash/caller id, ACTIVE token/user and strict expired_at > now;
                missing/inactive/revoked/expired/mismatched credentials is generic 401 E10002 with rollback before consent
                reads. No user/role/token locks or writes. This current credential gate preserves immediate logout/reset
                revocation (Q13).
            end note
            activate infra
            alt Read and mapping work completes
                note over app, infra
                    No locks or writes. Credentials, consent count and page use one repeatable-read snapshot.
                    Timeout or unexpected SQL/result/mapping failure may interrupt any step; no partial response.
                end note
                app -> app: Capture fresh server UTC now immediately before joined credential read; recheck JWT exp
                alt JWT expired before fresh credential read
                    break Reject this inquiry
                        app -> infra: ROLLBACK
                        app -> api: HTTP 401 E10002 Invalid or expired access token.
                        api -> page: Show failure without a partial consent page
                        page -> user: Display failure; no consent data
                    end break
                else Check passed
                end
                app -> infra: QUERY - Check current credential and user
                infra -> t_user_access_token: QUERY - Check current credential and user
                activate t_user_access_token
                    note right of t_user_access_token
                        SELECT
                            at.id as access_token_id
                        FROM authen.t_user_access_token at
                        JOIN authen.m_user u ON u.id = at.user_id
                        WHERE at.token = '<sequence.accessTokenHash>'
                        AND at.user_id = '<sequence.callerUserId>'
                        AND at.row_status = 'ACTIVE'
                        AND at.expired_at > '<sequence.now>'
                        AND u.row_status = 'ACTIVE'
                    end note
                    t_user_access_token -> infra: Return ACTIVE matching unexpired token/user or no row
                deactivate t_user_access_token
                infra -> app: Return ACTIVE matching unexpired token/user or no row
                alt Current token/user missing/inactive/revoked/expired/mismatched
                    break Reject this inquiry
                        app -> infra: ROLLBACK
                        app -> api: HTTP 401 E10002 Invalid or expired access token.
                        api -> page: Show failure without a partial consent page
                        page -> user: Display failure; no consent data
                    end break
                else Check passed
                end
                app -> app: Authorize once using exact case-sensitive PLATFORM_ADMIN in verified JWT roles; never reload current grants
                alt No exact PLATFORM_ADMIN role claim
                    break Reject this inquiry
                        app -> infra: ROLLBACK
                        app -> api: HTTP 403 E10009 You do not have permission to read consents.
                        api -> page: Show failure without a partial consent page
                        page -> user: Display failure; no consent data
                    end break
                else Check passed
                end
                app -> infra: QUERY - Get total items
                infra -> t_consent: QUERY - Get total items
                activate t_consent
                    note right of t_consent
                        SELECT
                            COUNT(c.id) as total_items
                        FROM consent.t_consent c
                        WHERE c.row_status <> 'DELETED'
                        AND ('<sequence.id>' IS NULL OR c.id = '<sequence.id>') -- only when id is specified
                        AND ('<sequence.searchPattern>' IS NULL OR c.code ILIKE '<sequence.searchPattern>' OR c.consent_name ILIKE '<sequence.searchPattern>' OR c.consent_description ILIKE '<sequence.searchPattern>') -- only when search is specified
                    end note
                    t_consent -> infra: Return totalItems for non-DELETED consents and all nullable filters
                deactivate t_consent
                infra -> app: Return totalItems for non-DELETED consents and all nullable filters
                app -> app: totalPages = 0 when totalItems=0, otherwise integer quotient plus nonzero remainder; no floating point or overflowing count+pageSize-1
                alt totalItems = 0
                    app -> app: items = []; skip page query; totalPages = 0
                else totalItems > 0
                    app -> infra: QUERY - Get consents
                    infra -> t_consent: QUERY - Get consents
                    activate t_consent
                        note right of t_consent
                            SELECT
                                c.id as consent_id,
                                c.code,
                                c.consent_type_id,
                                c.consent_version,
                                c.consent_name,
                                c.consent_description,
                                c.effective_at,
                                c.expired_at,
                                c.is_required,
                                c.row_status,
                                c.body
                            FROM consent.t_consent c
                            WHERE c.row_status <> 'DELETED'
                            AND ('<sequence.id>' IS NULL OR c.id = '<sequence.id>') -- only when id is specified
                            AND ('<sequence.searchPattern>' IS NULL OR c.code ILIKE '<sequence.searchPattern>' OR c.consent_name ILIKE '<sequence.searchPattern>' OR c.consent_description ILIKE '<sequence.searchPattern>') -- only when search is specified
                            ORDER BY c.created_at DESC, c.id
                            LIMIT '<sequence.pageSize>' OFFSET '<sequence.offset>'
                        end note
                        t_consent -> infra: Return consent rows in created_at descending/id order from identical filters/snapshot
                    deactivate t_consent
                    infra -> app: Return consent rows in created_at descending/id order from identical filters/snapshot
                    app -> app: Require page row count = min(pageSize, max(0, totalItems-offset)); mismatch is internal failure
                    alt Page contains rows
                        app -> app: consentTypeIds = typed UUID[] of the distinct consentTypeId values of the page rows
                        app -> infra: QUERY - Get consent type
                        infra -> m_consent_type: QUERY - Get consent type
                        activate m_consent_type
                            note right of m_consent_type
                                SELECT
                                    ct.id as consent_type_id,
                                    ct.name as consent_type_name
                                FROM consent.m_consent_type ct
                                WHERE ct.id = ANY ('<sequence.consentTypeIds>'::UUID[]) -- every status, Q19
                            end note
                            m_consent_type -> infra: Return consent type id/name rows of every status for the page
                        deactivate m_consent_type
                        infra -> app: Return consent type id/name rows of every status for the page
                        app -> app: Require exactly one type row per distinct consentTypeId; a missing type row is internal failure
                        app -> app: Map exactly consentId/code/consentTypeId/consentTypeName/consentVersion/consentName/consentDescription/effectiveAt/expiredAt/isRequired/rowStatus/body per row; expired and non-ACTIVE-type consents included; required values non-null; exclude caller/assignment/token/hash/audit
                    else Page beyond range contains no rows
                        app -> app: items = []; retain positive totalItems/totalPages; no 404
                    end
                end
                app -> app: data = exactly items/pageIndex/pageSize/totalItems/totalPages; echo validated page values; explicit empty arrays; finish full mapping
                app -> infra: COMMIT
                infra -> app: Return committed consistent read-only consent page
                note over app, infra
                    Approved by the product owner (Q18, 2026-11-09); use exact PLATFORM_ADMIN in verified JWT role claims under
                    [owner-confirmed review](../../../../../docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-07-api-review-design.md),
                    Q2/Q4/Q10/Q13. This detailed revision remains in-review; no backend/schema implementation. It does not
                    change the token-only consent type reference inquiry (consent/08) or the consumer consent lists.
                    Omitted searchPattern binds typed SQL NULL; supplied search, including empty string, becomes one bound text
                    searchPattern = percent + search + percent, preserving percent/underscore wildcards. Never interpolate
                    client text into SQL. The two nullable filters disable only themselves and combine by AND; id is still
                    filtered/paginated, not an unpaged alternate path.
                    After current credentials pass, authorize once using exact case-sensitive PLATFORM_ADMIN in verified JWT
                    roles. Valid roles=[] or any other role name is 403 E10009 `You do not have permission to read consents.`
                    after rollback and before count/page SQL. Never query current caller role assignments to grant, remove or
                    replace authorization. Grant withdrawal after token issuance leaves the old privilege usable until access
                    expiry (Q4); refresh reloads current grants (Q7).
                    **All consent records are returned (Q19, 2026-11-09).** Consents with rowStatus DELETED are never returned;
                    every other consent matching the filters is returned, including INACTIVE/LOCKED/ARCHIVED rows, consents
                    whose effective period has not started or has expired, and consents whose consent type is not ACTIVE. The
                    consumer visibility rules of consent/01 and consent/05 do not apply to this management list. No
                    historical-content storage is added: `body` is the stored current body.
                    Count first and optionally fetch the page in the same read-only repeatable-read snapshot as credentials.
                    Both consent queries use identical non-DELETED/id/searchPattern WHERE predicates; every supplied value is
                    bound, including pageSize and checked offset. If totalItems=0 skip the page SQL and return items=[],
                    totalPages=0. With positive count, query the requested page; an offset beyond the range returns items=[]
                    with positive totals/pages and no 404. A missing/DELETED id is the same empty-list 200 for an authorized
                    caller; permission is checked before revealing whether any consent exists.
                    When the page has rows, read the names of its distinct consent types with one bound typed UUID[] query in
                    the same snapshot, whatever the status of the type (Q19). A type row is mandatory by the foreign key: a
                    missing type row or a row count different from the distinct type ids is an internal failure. A page without
                    rows skips this query.
                    Sort by created_at descending, then id ascending (the existing newest-first order with a unique tie-breaker,
                    so pages never repeat or skip a row), preserving database collation. This is deterministic within one
                    snapshot; later requests may see newly committed changes and are not a frozen paging cursor.
                    Map each row to exactly
                    consentId/code/consentTypeId/consentTypeName/consentVersion/consentName/consentDescription/effectiveAt/expiredAt/isRequired/rowStatus/body.
                    No caller id, assignment, token/hash, audit or extra table fields are returned. Return exactly five data
                    keys: items/pageIndex/pageSize/totalItems/totalPages, with explicit empty arrays. Echo validated pages and
                    compute totalPages by integer quotient/remainder (zero when count=0), avoiding floating point or overflowing
                    count+pageSize-1. Require page row count = min(pageSize, max(0, totalItems-offset)); mismatch or
                    malformed/null/missing required data is internal failure.
                    Map the full response before COMMIT, then HTTP 200 S10000 Inquiry Consent Success. An unexpected
                    SQL/result/mapping error rolls back and returns generic 500 without bizCode; timeout before COMMIT rolls
                    back and returns 408 E90001. Never return partially mapped rows, mutate consents/assignments/tokens/audit,
                    or answer 404/409 for this inquiry.
                end note
                app -> api: HTTP 200 S10000 Inquiry Consent Success; all five pagination keys
                api -> page: Show authorized consent page and totals
                page -> user: Display consents or empty page
            else Timeout before COMMIT
                app -> infra: ROLLBACK
                app -> api: HTTP 408 E90001
                api -> page: Show failure without a partial consent page
                page -> user: Display failure; no consent data
            else Unexpected SQL/result/mapping failure before COMMIT
                app -> infra: ROLLBACK
                app -> api: HTTP 500 Internal Server Error; omit bizCode
                api -> page: Show failure without a partial consent page
                page -> user: Display failure; no consent data
            end
            deactivate infra
        deactivate app
    deactivate api
deactivate page
@enduml
